.TH CHTTPSVR_RESP_WRITE_JSON 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_resp_write_json \- append JSON to the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_resp_write_json(chttpsvr_resp *resp,
                                        const char *json, size_t len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends len bytes of json to the response body and then sets the
Content-Type response header to "application/json".  Because the body
is written first, resp does not change at all when the body
allocation runs out of memory: no header is installed and no bytes
are buffered.

When resp or json is NULL, or when len is 0, it returns
ccol_invalid_args at once and changes nothing in resp.  A zero-length
JSON body with the Content-Type header set has no valid meaning, so
the function rejects it instead of silently setting the header with
no body bytes.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - The body bytes were appended and the
                         Content-Type header was set.
ccol_invalid_args      - resp or json is NULL, or len is 0.
ccol_not_enough_memory - The allocation of the body buffer or of the
                         header buffer failed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_set_header (3)
